<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-060.5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Isotopic labelling The symbol for the isotope introduced is placed in square brackets directly attached to the part of the name to which it refers (e.g. sodium ('4C]formate); appropriate arabic numerals and prefixes are added as necessary (e.g. L-[2-C]leucine). For simple molecules, chemical formulae may be used (e.g. 4#CO,). Square brackets should not be used when the isotopic symbol is attached to a word that is not a chemical name (e.g. “!*C-labelled”). Terms such as “'![-labelled albumin” should not be contracted to [3!T]albumin since native albumin does not contain iodine." <https://iris.who.int/graph/community/5bff2c18-6c2b-4658-9087-93811d2399c0> .
<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-060.5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/Work> <https://iris.who.int/graph/community/5bff2c18-6c2b-4658-9087-93811d2399c0> .
