<https://litlfred.github.io/folio/references/who-pub-tps-931.page-064-2.9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Interleukins Designations have been officially adopted for 17 interleukins: interleukin-1 to interleukin-16, including interleukin-lo and interleukin-1B. These terms are generally abbreviated IL-1a, IL-5, IL-13, etc. Forther reading IUIS/WHO Standing Committee on Interleukin Designation. Nomenclature for secreted regulatory proteins of the immune system (Interleukins): update. Bulletin of the World Health Organization, 1997, 75:175." <https://iris.who.int/graph/community/5bff2c18-6c2b-4658-9087-93811d2399c0> .
